      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could these dependency checks run before add_vpp_plugin()? The plugin target has already been created when a check returns. With the libnl-genl-3 development library missing, configuration reports that FastACL is disabled, but the build still compiles fastacl_psample.c and fails because the libnl include path was never added.",
      "revId": "f8354c8fcf7bc31d703982c68821f4f513fe61ed",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8479c37_abbccb70",
        "filename": "src/plugins/fastacl/fastacl.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 203,
      "author": {
        "id": 361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T08:40:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we clear enabled_interfaces when an interface is deleted? VPP removes its feature configuration, but this bitmap remains set. If a replacement interface reuses the index, enabling FastACL returns success here without attaching the filter nodes. I reproduced this by deleting and recreating an enabled loopback.",
      "revId": "f8354c8fcf7bc31d703982c68821f4f513fe61ed",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4df2a1d2_396a1b47",
        "filename": "src/plugins/fastacl/fastacl_node.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T08:40:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this condition be frag_off !\u003d 0? RFC 8955/8956 define IsF as a fragment other than the first. Including mf also sets it on first fragments, causing an IsF drop rule to discard them. I reproduced this with IPv4 first fragments.",
      "revId": "f8354c8fcf7bc31d703982c68821f4f513fe61ed",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ea21c573_e757992b",
        "filename": "src/plugins/fastacl/fastacl_node.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 151,
      "author": {
        "id": 361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T08:40:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we use the complete IP packet length for matching, separately from the bounds used to access headers? avail covers only the first buffer, so chained packets are classified with a truncated length. I reproduced 5,028-byte IPv4 packets bypassing a 5000–6000 drop rule. The IPv6 parser has the same issue.",
      "revId": "f8354c8fcf7bc31d703982c68821f4f513fe61ed",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24eea485_d5752a44",
        "filename": "src/plugins/fastacl/fastacl_node.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T08:40:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we preserve the protocol identified by the Fragment Header here? Assigning protocol 44 makes noninitial UDP fragments bypass a proto 17 drop rule, even though their Fragment Header identifies UDP. I reproduced this with first fragments being dropped and later fragments being forwarded. Transport fields should remain unavailable for noninitial fragments.",
      "revId": "f8354c8fcf7bc31d703982c68821f4f513fe61ed",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
